The attached image illustrates the strong adjuvant effect of Nano-11, an alpha-D-glucan nanoparticle, on enhancing antibody responses to recombinant protective antigen (rPA). The box-and-whisker plot shows that mice immunized with rPA alone developed very low anti-rPA IgG titers. In contrast, formulations containing rPA with either aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11 significantly increased antibody titers. Notably, Nano-11 at all tested doses (200, 50, and 12.5 µg) induced high antibody levels comparable to or exceeding those achieved with higher doses of AH, demonstrating superior immunopotentiation, particularly at lower concentrations.